      "message": "Hi,\nThe patch-set 2 adds a new ocnfig to handle the 4-byte case of Port80 code.\nIt will group 4-byte data into a single variable and pass it to port.c in common code.\nNote that the common port80 code assumes that the Port80 code \u003c 0x100 and the array \"history\" is only uint16_t. I cannot see the console print the grouped code with \"#define CONFIG_PORT80_PRINT_IN_INT 0\"\nIf \"#define CONFIG_PORT80_PRINT_IN_INT 1\", the grouped code can be printed correctly like:\n[4743.660839 Port 80: 0xeee20400]\n",
